ok the request line is split
ok the query string is kept apart from the path
ok query decodes + and names
ok header names are case-insensitive
ok a GET has an empty body
ok the body is read to Content-Length
ok form groups a nested prefix
ok form_value reads a top-level field
ok form of an absent prefix is empty
ok a non-form body is not decoded as a form
ok EOF before a request line is nil
ok a malformed request line is 400
ok a request target without a leading slash is 400
ok a header without a colon is 400
ok headers past 8 KB are 431
ok a body past 1 MB is 413
ok a non-numeric Content-Length is 400
ok a body shorter than Content-Length is 400
ok a chunked body is 400
ok headers cut off by EOF are 400
ok broken percent-encoding in a form is BadRequest
ok broken percent-encoding in a query is BadRequest
ok path_int reads digits
ok path_int of letters is BadRequest
ok path_int of a huge number is BadRequest, not an overflow
ok path_int of a missing param is BadRequest
ok override_method changes the verb
ok Form.encode round-trips through decode
